{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": "Synthetic Gen1 mechanic vectors for Lua/JS BattleSim parity. No ROM data: no species, move, ability or item names appear here, only integer ids and type indices 0..15. All arithmetic is integer; floor() truncates toward zero and every value is an integer, boolean or null (never NaN). DAMAGE. statClamp: if attack > 255 or defense > 255 then both become max(1, floor(x/4)). levelTerm = floor(2*L/5 + 2), where L = level*2 on a critical hit (so crit doubles the level term rather than the final damage). base = floor(floor(levelTerm * power * attack / defense) / 50) + 2. STAB is floor(d*3/2). Type effectiveness is a list of percents applied one at a time as floor(d * pct / 100), matching Gen1 per-type application. If any percent is 0 the attack is immune: damage is 0 and no further step runs. Otherwise the random factor is damage = max(1, floor(d * roll / 255)) with roll in 217..255; the min-1 clamp is always applied (this fixture does not model the Gen1 \"skip the roll when damage is 1\" shortcut). Cases with roll: null assert the full band via minDamage/maxDamage inclusive. ACCURACY. accuracy, accuracyMod and evasionMod are 0..255 and percents respectively. effectiveAccuracy = clamp(floor(floor(accuracy * accuracyMod / 100) * evasionMod / 100), 1, 255) and hit = roll < effectiveAccuracy for roll in 0..255. Because roll has 256 values and effectiveAccuracy caps at 255, a \"100%\" move still misses 1/256 of the time (roll 255). alwaysHits: true bypasses the roll entirely and reports effectiveAccuracy: null. CRIT. threshold = floor(baseSpeed / 2); focusEnergy quarters it (floor(t/4)) reproducing the Gen1 bug rather than raising it; a high-critical-ratio move multiplies by 8; the result is clamped to 0..255. isCrit = roll < threshold for roll in 0..255, so a threshold of 255 still fails on roll 255 and a threshold of 0 never crits. STATUS. Sleep decrements the counter before the move and the waking turn is still lost. Paralysis stops the turn when roll < 63 (63/256) and quarters speed as max(1, floor(speed/4)). Freeze never self-thaws in Gen1, so thawed is false for every roll. Burn and poison deal max(1, floor(maxHp/16)) per turn; burn also halves attack as max(1, floor(attack/2)). Toxic deals max(1, floor(maxHp/16)) * toxicCounter. Confusion decrements its counter first, snaps out at 0, and otherwise self-hits when roll < 128 (50%) for a typeless 40-power hit using the confused side own attack and defense with no STAB, no type effectiveness and no crit, at a fixed roll of 255.",
